From 25532fda1bc0d26e49c115f7742ce59fc63963aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nex <63727521+LuCiLuna@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:37:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 016/114] WIP: drm/panel: add Samsung AMB670YF01 and enable MSM
 DSI on OnePlus 9 Pro

DSC command mode panel behind the Pixelworks Iris (left in analog bypass
by the bootloader). Init sequence generated from the vendor fhd_sdc_60
timing. Runs DSC at 8 bpc (10 bpc renders dark greys far too bright with
msm) and widens hfp so the derived DSI rate matches the vendor
825.6 Mbps/lane. Includes a debugfs DCS read/write interface for bring-up.

Known issue: lit pixels pulse in brightness on every sparse frame update
(panel self-refresh vs host write); a continuous frame stream hides it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
